#### Consolidated content for the v2 single-page tool (dev-plan §3.6). ####
#### Copy landed 2026-08-20 from e2w_refresh_text_DHreview.md. ####

#### TITLE / HERO ####

title: The Education-to-Workforce Framework Data Tool

description: Explore data on education and workforce outcomes, and compare data by geography, income, race, ethnicity, and more.

data_download_link: https://datacatalog.urban.org/dataset/education-workforce-framework-tool-data

data_download_text: Download Data

[copy]
* The path from school to the workforce has no set route, which can make measuring short-term milestones and long-term outcomes difficult. To ensure students are headed in the right direction and have access to environments that set them up for success, local leaders need data that span across sectors and systems.
* The <a href="https://educationtoworkforce.org/" target="_blank">Education-to-Workforce Indicator Framework</a> makes it easy <a href="https://thetraininghub.strivetogether.org/learn/courses/541/introduction-to-the-e-w-framework-self-paced" target="_blank">to understand students’ performance and progress</a> across geographies and over time. Here, we collect all available national data to allow policymakers, educators, community organizations, parents, and students to measure achievement and take action in their communities.
[]

