#### "HOW TO INTERPRET THIS TOOL" MODAL ####
#### copy is an ordered list of blocks; `type` picks the element (p | list). ####

{modal}
title: How to interpret this tool

[.copy]
type: p
value: This tool displays three components of the <a href="https://educationtoworkforce.org/" target="_blank">Education-to-Workforce Indicator Framework</a>:

type: list
[.items]
* <strong>Essential questions</strong> frame how stakeholders can measure performance and progress in their community. The framework includes 20 essential questions, which can be answered by the indicators of success.
* <strong>Indicators of success</strong> identify metrics that track milestones, outcomes, and local conditions. The framework includes 99 indicators of success, each of which identifies one or more metrics. Together, the indicators provide a holistic picture of education and workforce systems.
* <strong>Disaggregates</strong> show any disparities in outcomes across student characteristics. The framework identifies 26 disaggregates, 7 of which we display.
[]

type: p
value: Select an essential question to explore indicators of success, metrics, and disaggregates. You can also use the map to view different metrics and geographic levels.
[]
{}

