#### SHARED AVAILABILITY PHRASE ####
#### "{n} metrics across {m} indicators of success" — used verbatim by the EQ heading, the
#### all-data subtitle and the unavailable-data heading, so the three read the same way.
#### The two nouns pluralize independently: an essential question can have several metrics
#### under a single indicator, so one shared singular form would render "2 metric across
#### 1 indicator". `templateNoCount` is for the layout that renders the number separately.

{availability}
template: {{metricCount}} {{metricNoun}} across {{indicatorCount}} {{indicatorNoun}}
templateNoCount: {{metricNoun}} across {{indicatorCount}} {{indicatorNoun}}
metricNoun: metrics
metricNounSingular: metric
indicatorNoun: indicators of success
indicatorNounSingular: indicator of success
availableSuffix: have available data
availableSuffixSingular: has available data
unavailableSuffix: for {{eqName}} do not have available data
unavailableSuffixSingular: for {{eqName}} does not have available data
noneAvailable: No metrics have available data
{}

#### EQ SECTION (jump link + drawers) ####

{eqSection}
learnMoreLabel: About This Essential Question
#### the per-EQ intro and use-case sentences live in essential-questions.aml; this middle ####
#### sentence is shared, and {{count}} is the EQ's indicator_list length ####
learnMoreCountTemplate: To answer this question, the Education-to-Workforce Framework identifies {{count}} indicators of success:
populationLabel: Local Population Characteristics
populationLabelNational: National Population Characteristics
